= August 2021 — The governing majority frays

[? if porozumienie_exit_done = 1: Prime Minister <span class="party-pis"><b>Mateusz Morawiecki</b></span> has dismissed his deputy and Porozumienie leader **Jarosław Gowin**, and **[+ porozumienie_seats +]** Porozumienie deputies have followed him out of the United Right; the rest chose their places on the PiS benches. The cabinet is still standing, but its majority is no longer an agreement. It is Kaczyński's discipline, a few unaffiliated votes and a fresh count before every difficult bill.?]
[? if porozumienie_exit_done = 0: The coalition survived its August. Gowin is still a deputy prime minister and Porozumienie is still inside the United Right, which means the government's majority is intact on paper and conditional in practice: it now depends on a partner who has demonstrated that he will make it public when he is refused.?]

Gowin says the Polish Deal's tax provisions made the break unavoidable after
the earlier revolt over the postal election. PiS calls it betrayal. Our whips
hear something more useful in the recriminations: Morawiecki needs votes, and
after the recovery-fund bargain he knows that some of ours may have a price.

KO wants to put a replacement government to the test. Trade unionists and
hospital organisers want concessions while the cabinet is weak. Meanwhile,
Konfederacja is turning anger at pandemic restrictions into recruits. For once
the question is not whether Lewica has leverage, but how much responsibility
we are prepared to take for using it.

[? if pis_relation >= 50 and government_negotiation_hostility <= 50: Months of
quiet social-policy talks have produced an offer nobody expected to hear.
Kaczyński will concede Labour, Housing and Health if the New Left club gives
Morawiecki a majority. Razem has already said it will not take the oath.?]

